# Edit existing files — do not create extras

Whenever possible, fix problems by **changing contents of files that already exist**. Do not create new files, plugins, snippets, wrappers, or docs as a workaround.

## Rule of thumb

1. Name the **existing** path (repo and/or live SiteGround path).
2. Say **exactly which contents** must change (field, function, string, block).
3. Prefer overwrite / paste into that file over adding a sibling file.
4. New files only when the user explicitly asks, or when no existing file can hold the change.

## Examples

| Situation | Do this | Not this |
|---|---|---|
| Contact page broken | Edit live `wp-content/plugins/wrrapd-contact-hub/wrrapd-contact-hub.php` (same content as repo `wordpress/wrrapd-contact-hub-plugin.php`) | New MU plugin, new page, or new HTML file |
| CWS listing text | Edit that item’s Store listing / Privacy fields | New store item or new support page |
| Extension update | Upload zip on the **existing** item’s Package tab | New Item |
| Copy / CSS fix | Patch the existing PHP/CSS that already owns it | New “fix” stylesheet or one-shot plugin |

## Agent replies

Lead with the file path and the content change. Do not open with “create a new file” unless nothing else works, and say so explicitly.
